<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>News from Europe - Latest world headlines and daily news - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24 explores events across Europe, including in the 27 member states of the European Union and the United Kingdom. Follow our on-the-ground reports, interviews and analyses of the events affecting social and political life on the Continent and Europe’s role in the world.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/</link><lastBuildDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 05:00:45 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Europe</category><title>Live: Curfews come into effect in Paris and other French cities after rioting</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261020-live-curfews-come-into-effect-around-france-to-combat-looting</link><description>
Curfews came into effect in cities across France, including parts of Paris, Bordeaux, Nice and Lyon, as French police attempted to crack down on rioting and looting during protests. Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu has said that implementing a state of emergency is not out of the question. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4ba3c65c-cc29-11f1-b901-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3RV38Z.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4ba3c65c-cc29-11f1-b901-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3RV38Z.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2b1c7b6a-cc31-11f1-b8dd-5384bc80ef02</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:51:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4ba3c65c-cc29-11f1-b901-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3RV38Z.jpg">© Olivier Chassignole, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Zelensky accuses US of delaying missile deliveries as tensions rise</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261020-zelensky-accuses-us-of-delaying-missile-deliveries-as-tensions-rise</link><description>
Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky accused the US on Monday of holding up deliveries of Patriot interceptor missiles already paid for by European allies, as tensions with President Donald Trump’s administration deepened over military aid and intelligence sharing.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/35a106a0-cbdc-11f1-844f-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/bb914f42bdf0a8c35c60195688087ff485fa414d.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/35a106a0-cbdc-11f1-844f-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/bb914f42bdf0a8c35c60195688087ff485fa414d.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">89de3ff6-cc29-11f1-a926-d518a0f5c63b</guid><pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 01:56:59 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/35a106a0-cbdc-11f1-844f-d1d2c32ebb87/w:1024/p:16x9/bb914f42bdf0a8c35c60195688087ff485fa414d.jpg">© Oleskii Filippov, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Spain floods kill four as torrential rain inundates eastern regions</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261019-spain-floods-kill-four-as-torrential-rain-inundates-eastern-regions</link><description>
Torrential rain battered eastern Spain on Monday, killing at least four people in recent days as floodwaters swept away cars, submerged roads and stranded residents. Emergency crews carried out more than 400 rescues in Valencia, where rainfall reached 700 litres per square metre in 24 hours in some areas.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e9c067e8-b287-11f1-a41a-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T090156Z-1967335667-RC2UKNAXSDKS-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-SPAIN-FLOODS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e9c067e8-b287-11f1-a41a-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T090156Z-1967335667-RC2UKNAXSDKS-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-SPAIN-FLOODS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9cd79e50-cc05-11f1-b217-5541766e675c</guid><pubDate>Mon, 19 Oct 2026 21:39:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e9c067e8-b287-11f1-a41a-991cccd3bb73/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-17T090156Z-1967335667-RC2UKNAXSDKS-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-SPAIN-FLOODS.jpg">© Eva Manez, Reuters,</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Russia-China-US summit would prolong the war, Kyiv says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/russia-china-us-summit-would-prolong-the-war-kyiv-says</link><description>
Ukrainian ⁠Foreign Minister ​Andrii Sybiha said on ​Monday that a summit between Russia, China ​and the ‌US would ⁠encourage President Vladimir Putin ‌to prolong the war. The ​Wall Street Journal reported that Putin had proposed a ​summit next month ​with US ​President Donald Trump and Chinese President ​Xi Jinping to negotiate an end to the war on terms ⁠that would favour Moscow. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/49054872-cbf1-11f1-ac7d-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261019-204634-204832-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/49054872-cbf1-11f1-ac7d-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261019-204634-204832-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4e213032-cbf1-11f1-acc3-b5be01021aca</guid><pubDate>Mon, 19 Oct 2026 19:21:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Zelensky says Starshield speed limits slowing down frontline response</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/zelensky-says-starshield-speed-limits-slowing-down-frontline-response</link><description>
Speed limits on a US military grade satellite system are hindering Ukrainian forces' ability to coordinate drone strikes against Russian forces, President Volodymyr Zelensky said on Monday. Zelensky said frontline units had reported that the Starshield equipment "stops functioning at speeds of 130-160 kilometres (80-100 miles) per hour in various sectors of the front". Separately, a Ukrainian army brigade has announced the rescue of a wounded soldier from the front line using an aerial drone, describing the evacuation as the first of its kind. The brigade published a video showing the drone lowering itself to the ground, before a man in combat gear fastens himself to a winch onboard and is lifted upwards. FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg reports from Ukraine.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5b2ff02a-cbeb-11f1-aa78-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261019-201534-202025-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5b2ff02a-cbeb-11f1-aa78-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261019-201534-202025-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">60c6f718-cbeb-11f1-9d3b-059ce88594d7</guid><pubDate>Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:45:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ukraine deploys drone to airlift wounded soldier in 'world-first' operation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261019-ukraine-deploys-drone-airlift-wounded-soldier-world-first-operation</link><description>

 
Ukraine has evacuated a wounded soldier from the front line using an aerial drone in what a Ukrainian army brigade has described as a world-first operation. The successful mission highlights the growing role of unmanned technology in battlefield evacuations as drones continue to shape the conflict between Ukraine and Russia.
 

 

 

</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/535361e8-cbd2-11f1-b00b-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26288408031156.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/535361e8-cbd2-11f1-b00b-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26288408031156.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bc9617ec-cbd0-11f1-9bfe-01d4bc45be7d</guid><pubDate>Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:44:42 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/535361e8-cbd2-11f1-b00b-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26288408031156.jpg">© Evgeniy Maloletk, AP Photo</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Quite horrifying': Afghan economic crisis leaves EU deportees with 'very little' to return to</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261019-quite-horrifying-afghan-economic-crisis-leaves-eu-deportees-with-very-little-to-return-to-1</link><description>
Europe's increasingly pragmatic engagement with Afghanistan's Taliban rulers is exposing a fundamental contradiction between diplomatic non-recognition and political necessity. In an investigation for The New York Times, Pakistan and Afghanistan bureau chief Elian Peltier reveals how European governments are quietly expanding negotiations with the Taliban over migrant deportations, diplomatic representation and economic assistance. “Even though on paper European governments do not recognise the Taliban administration, in practice they meet much more frequently than most of us know,” Peltier explains. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ed5ea6e8-cb83-11f1-ad1d-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-080919-081512-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ed5ea6e8-cb83-11f1-ad1d-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261013-080919-081512-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f2d2a4ee-cb83-11f1-8efe-3324605fe5d3</guid><pubDate>Mon, 19 Oct 2026 06:33:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Russia pounds Kyiv as Rubio urges Ukraine's Zelensky to 'focus' on ending war</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261019-live-russian-strikes-pound-kyiv-as-rubio-denies-us-paused-intel-sharing-with-ukraine</link><description>
Russia on Monday said it carried out a "massive strike" on targets in Kyiv and its region as US Secretary of State Marco Rubio denied that Washington had paused intelligence sharing with Ukraine and urged its President Volodymyr Zelensky to focus on ending the war.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bf71a96e-cb7f-11f1-8810-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-18T235422Z-1304641961-RC2X5OA93ZJS-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bf71a96e-cb7f-11f1-8810-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-18T235422Z-1304641961-RC2X5OA93ZJS-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9c12fa3e-cb81-11f1-a0b8-156ee1be6e64</guid><pubDate>Mon, 19 Oct 2026 06:00:06 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bf71a96e-cb7f-11f1-8810-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-18T235422Z-1304641961-RC2X5OA93ZJS-RTRMADP-3-UKRAINE-CRISIS-ATTACK-KYIV.jpg">© Valentyn Ogirenko, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Zelensky holds US talks as Trump accuses him of not wanting peace</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261018-ukraine-zelensky-war-trump-peace-russia-sanctions</link><description>
Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky spoke with US envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner on Sunday amid tensions after US President Donald Trump accused Kyiv of resisting peace with Russia. The talks came as both sides exchanged attacks on energy infrastructure, while Washington's easing of Russian sanctions raised concerns among European allies.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c4a57392-8d19-11f1-9ad5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3EB39E-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c4a57392-8d19-11f1-9ad5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3EB39E-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4772322c-cb38-11f1-90fd-e7219516a3d1</guid><pubDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:59:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c4a57392-8d19-11f1-9ad5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C3EB39E-1.jpg">© Ukrainian Presidential Press Service, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ukrainian drone attack on Saint Petersburg kills one, sets refinery ablaze</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261018-ukraine-sets-saint-petersburg-refinery-ablaze-in-large-scale-drone-attack</link><description>
A large-scale Ukrainian drone attack on Russia's second-largest city Saint Petersburg killed at least one person and hospitalised another five on Sunday. The attack – which also sparked fires at an oil refinery and depot – comes as Kyiv accused Russia of violating Washington's "energy ceasefire" dozens of times.   
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c0e82312-cae0-11f1-8a5c-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/08624102e36095dfc5692eadfc7780474a0d2bb4.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c0e82312-cae0-11f1-8a5c-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/08624102e36095dfc5692eadfc7780474a0d2bb4.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">eb34469a-caeb-11f1-8a26-67c23fcd3799</guid><pubDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 12:03:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c0e82312-cae0-11f1-8a5c-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/08624102e36095dfc5692eadfc7780474a0d2bb4.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Macron denounces 'unbridled' violence as France hit by new clashes</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261018-live-vance-blames-immigration-for-violence-during-protests-in-france</link><description>
President Emmanuel Macron on Sunday slammed the "unbridled" violence that erupted in cost-of-living protests across France, as police battled protesters and looters in new clashes in Paris. Nearly 2,400 people were arrested and at least 1,000 police and gendarmes injured, the interior ministry said. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/65d6e4e8-cb23-11f1-a601-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-18T183457Z-1777343427-RC2U5OAGNYMW-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-PROTEST.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/65d6e4e8-cb23-11f1-a601-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-18T183457Z-1777343427-RC2U5OAGNYMW-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-PROTEST.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">537a7882-caa1-11f1-a119-73fa622837ec</guid><pubDate>Sun, 18 Oct 2026 03:09:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/65d6e4e8-cb23-11f1-a601-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-18T183457Z-1777343427-RC2U5OAGNYMW-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-PROTEST.jpg">© Manon Cruz, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Pope Leo returns to Vatican four days after lung cancer surgery</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261017-pope-leo-returns-to-vatican-four-days-after-lung-cancer-surgery</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV was released from the hospital on Saturday after lung cancer surgery. Doctors removed part of the 71-year-old's right lung last week to extract a cancerous tumour. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/745c4444-ca16-11f1-81af-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/5eefb12dbc48266fba95f0685a09134b43ef53d7.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/745c4444-ca16-11f1-81af-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/5eefb12dbc48266fba95f0685a09134b43ef53d7.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7516321e-ca16-11f1-a401-2d75c047ea6f</guid><pubDate>Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:35:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/745c4444-ca16-11f1-81af-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/5eefb12dbc48266fba95f0685a09134b43ef53d7.jpg">© Tiziana Fabi, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Zelensky fears Trump 'will continue' to lift Russia sanctions</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-zelensky-turns-to-europe-for-backing-as-ties-with-trump-deteriorate</link><description>
Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said on Saturday that he feared his US counterpart Donald Trump "will continue" lifitng sanctions on Russia. Zelensky's relationship with Trump deteriorated after the Washington eased sanctions on Moscow as part of a diesel-supply deal, despite Russia increasing strikes on Ukraine. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c6338998-c99a-11f1-9ea4-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3GY8H7.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c6338998-c99a-11f1-9ea4-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3GY8H7.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c0dc235e-c99c-11f1-b230-09bd13f05fa4</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:25:46 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c6338998-c99a-11f1-9ea4-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3GY8H7.jpg">© Nicolas Tucat, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>'Finish what we started': After student protests, France braces for return of the Yellow Vests</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-finish-what-we-started-after-student-protests-france-braces-return-yellow-vests</link><description>
An online movement against rising fuel prices has gained momentum ahead of planned nationwide demonstrations on October 17 with former Yellow Vest figures set to join the protests in support of high-school students. Some are drawing parallels between the latest action and the 2018 cost-of-living protests that rattled President Emmanuel Macron's first term in office.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a84b63e-c8a0-11f1-ac1f-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-1GD2EZ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a84b63e-c8a0-11f1-ac1f-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-1GD2EZ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">97200a1c-c960-11f1-b0c0-219ae52178dc</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:10:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7a84b63e-c8a0-11f1-ac1f-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-1GD2EZ.jpg">© Jean-Philippe Ksiazek, AFP</source><dc:creator>Grégoire SAUVAGE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Clashes grip Tirana as Albanian PM blames 'foreign hands' for mounting unrest</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-clashes-grip-tirana-as-albanian-pm-blames-foreign-hands</link><description>
Albanian Prime Minister Edi Rama on Friday blamed the involvement of “foreign hands” for escalating protests, which he said are aimed at hindering Albania's bid to join the European Union. Thousands of demonstrators have taken to the streets of Albania's capital since Tuesday, demanding Rama’s resignation and denouncing university conditions and high tuition fees.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/14fcd6c8-c99c-11f1-9d93-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/6444105dfca67f7f4b62d440579b190d86972ee5.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/14fcd6c8-c99c-11f1-9d93-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/6444105dfca67f7f4b62d440579b190d86972ee5.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">15a18646-c99c-11f1-b372-e3f3ed909f1f</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 19:59:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/14fcd6c8-c99c-11f1-9d93-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/6444105dfca67f7f4b62d440579b190d86972ee5.jpg">© Adnan Beci, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The World This Week</category><title>Trump vs Zelensky, From the screen to the streets, Gen Z protests from Paris to Dehli</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20261016-trump-vs-zelensky-from-the-screen-to-the-streets-gen-z-protests-from-paris-to-dehli</link><description>
Our panel of international correspondents look back at the week's news, from protests in India to a blame game in Ukraine.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3790a46a-ca34-11f1-a355-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/Trump-et-Zelenskyy-portraits-en-contraste.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3790a46a-ca34-11f1-a355-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/Trump-et-Zelenskyy-portraits-en-contraste.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e58b69a0-c995-11f1-b872-dd39bf954344</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 19:21:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>'US tilting toward Russia: Europeans are standing more and more solidly with Zelensky'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261016-us-tilting-toward-russia-europeans-are-standing-more-and-more-solidly-with-zelensky</link><description>
As transatlantic relations confront renewed geopolitical uncertainty, former Estonian president Toomas Hendrik Ilves delivers a pointed assessment of Washington's shifting approach to Russia's war on Ukraine and the profound implications for European security. At the heart of his analysis lies a fundamental question: can Europe develop the political unity, strategic independence and military capabilities necessary to defend its interests in an increasingly unpredictable international order? Ilves' response: "If there's any time for Europe to begin to act as Europe and not as being strictly self-interested, then this is the time for it."
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3cd7696-cbc7-11f1-be95-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a3a0b1ff.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a3cd7696-cbc7-11f1-be95-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a3a0b1ff.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0c6d977e-c990-11f1-865b-e5ec033cc9b6</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 18:33:13 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>The 51%</category><title>The risks faced by women migrants in Europe</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-51/20261016-the-risks-faced-by-women-migrants-in-europe</link><description>
This October marks 10 years since French police dismantled the notorious Calais "Jungle" camp. FRANCE 24's Claire Paccalin returns to the region to explore what has changed for migrants over the past decade. She joins Annette Young and Dr Marissa Quie of Cambridge University to discuss migration routes and their growing role in European political debate.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ef69a52-c952-11f1-91fd-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/pic-web.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ef69a52-c952-11f1-91fd-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/pic-web.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">82a91212-c952-11f1-b7c0-f3512f0888e9</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:05:20 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Annette YOUNG</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Pope Leo XIV celebrates mass in hospital while recovering from lung cancer operation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-pope-leo-xiv-celebrates-mass-in-hospital-while-recovering-from-lung-cancer-operation</link><description>
Pope Leo XIV celebrated a mass at Rome's Gemelli hospital Friday after undergoing surgery to remove a cancerous tumour from his right lung, photos released by the Vatican showed. Doctors said his recovery was progressing normally but that further tests would show whether the cancer had spread.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/20a78260-c961-11f1-a208-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/b9a198cac6936ae44ee5b8c08a3fe4152c41404a.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/20a78260-c961-11f1-a208-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/b9a198cac6936ae44ee5b8c08a3fe4152c41404a.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">216586d4-c961-11f1-8b74-219ae52178dc</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:57:23 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/20a78260-c961-11f1-a208-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/b9a198cac6936ae44ee5b8c08a3fe4152c41404a.jpg">© Vatican media handout via AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>'America, with this president, is not our ally. Trump is a liar': French MEP Bernard Guetta</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261016-america-with-this-president-is-not-our-ally-trump-is-a-liar-french-mep-bernard-guetta</link><description>
Our guest is veteran French journalist and commentator Bernard Guetta, who is a Member of the European Parliament for the centrist Renew group. He tells the programme that Donald Trump is "a liar, because he tried to tell the American people that Zelensky and the Ukrainian resistance were responsible for the price of diesel. This is a pure lie. He (Trump) is responsible because he started the war with Iran." Guetta goes on to say that "without American intelligence sharing, Ukraine is weaker and weaker. That's terrible, to see the president of the United States giving a hand to Putin against Ukraine."
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54ceab9e-c8a4-11f1-b31f-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/ENTK-TALKING-EU1-GUETTA-261017-2027-Ep-7-transfer.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54ceab9e-c8a4-11f1-b31f-6313a763b466/w:1024/p:16x9/ENTK-TALKING-EU1-GUETTA-261017-2027-Ep-7-transfer.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">15b7bc28-c653-11f1-8f3d-97eea9bcf669</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:55:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Armen GEORGIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Talking Europe</category><title>EU and Canada seek closer ties: Will Canada become the EU's first associate member?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20261016-eu-and-canada-seek-closer-ties-will-canada-become-the-eu-s-first-associate-member</link><description>
As the international context becomes more challenging for the European Union, the bloc is looking to boost its ties with like-minded allies. Canada is part of that architecture that the EU says it wants to build. The big news of EU Commission President Ursula von der Leyen's State of the Union speech in September was that Canada could become an associate member – an arrangement that does not exist for the EU's partners at the moment.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0ee425ac-c893-11f1-84f5-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/261014-FR24-Talking-EU-1-div.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0ee425ac-c893-11f1-84f5-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/261014-FR24-Talking-EU-1-div.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8de8b97c-c653-11f1-9540-3fc578080398</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 12:04:22 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Armen GEORGIAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>UK bookstores scramble as Sally Rooney's novels pulled over Palestine Action support</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-uk-bookstores-scramble-as-sally-rooney-novels-pulled-over-palestine-action-support</link><description>
Critically acclaimed Irish novelist Sally Rooney's announcement that her books could no longer be sold in the UK due to her support for proscribed group Palestine Action has left British booksellers rushing to stock up on her works before distributors run out. The British government's ban on the group, which practiced non-violent direct action and sabotage against UK military assets believed to be working with the Israeli government, makes support for Palestine Action punishable by up to 14 years in prison.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0420bd06-c924-11f1-923c-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-14T151142Z-1755491356-RC233OAKW8RS-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-SALLY-ROONEY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0420bd06-c924-11f1-923c-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-14T151142Z-1755491356-RC233OAKW8RS-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-SALLY-ROONEY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">206a3ea2-c923-11f1-809f-7bc78db3cd1e</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 06:15:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0420bd06-c924-11f1-923c-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-14T151142Z-1755491356-RC233OAKW8RS-RTRMADP-3-BRITAIN-SALLY-ROONEY.jpg">© Henry Nicholls, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Ukraine's backers will 'be looking at' Kyiv's €70 billion request, Macron says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-live-trump-calls-renewed-ukraine-attacks-on-russian-oil-refineries-a-disgrace</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron said the EU will “not abandon Ukraine and the Ukrainian people” and that Kyiv’s request for extra funds will be examined, while addressing the media at a summit in Brussels Friday. Earlier, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky asked EU leaders to provide Kyiv with an extra €70 billion next year to help with the country's ongoing fight against Russia. Read about the day’s events as they unfolded on our liveblog. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5ade75ba-c984-11f1-b407-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3J24W6.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5ade75ba-c984-11f1-b407-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3J24W6.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ec95e172-c903-11f1-b093-3b96d215f849</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 01:50:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5ade75ba-c984-11f1-b407-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D3J24W6.jpg">© Ludovic Marin, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Minibus crashes into train at French Channel Tunnel entrance, injuring 19</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261016-19-injured-as-minibus-crashes-into-train-at-channel-tunnel-entrance</link><description>
Nineteen people were injured Thursday when a minibus carrying truck drivers crashed into a vehicle shuttle train at the French entrance to the Channel Tunnel near Calais, forcing a 90-minute suspension of shuttle services. Two people were hospitalised with serious but non-life-threatening injuries, French authorities said.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a8daece-71cc-11f0-9526-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-397M8WK.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a8daece-71cc-11f0-9526-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-397M8WK.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f99b5af8-c8fb-11f1-b305-c7c144120c8c</guid><pubDate>Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:53:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6a8daece-71cc-11f0-9526-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-397M8WK.jpg">© Sameer Al-Doumy, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>France and Germany agree to ease EU car emissions rules in new deal</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-france-and-germany-agree-to-ease-eu-car-emissions-rules-in-new-deal</link><description>
Paris and Berlin on Friday confirmed their deal aimed at protecting Europe's struggling automotive sector, having reached agreements on the flashpoint issues of EU car emissions and "made in Europe" components. A draft deal reviewed Thursday showed the two countries backing looser EU emissions rules for carmakers.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af286218-c8e7-11f1-8247-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26270718148994.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af286218-c8e7-11f1-8247-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26270718148994.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fd324f7c-c8f2-11f1-a500-2b19cb1aea8f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:48:57 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/af286218-c8e7-11f1-8247-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26270718148994.jpg">© Michael Sohn, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Europe</category><title>Zelensky rallies European allies as US support for Ukraine wanes</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-zelensky-rallies-european-allies-as-us-support-for-ukraine-wanes</link><description>
Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky sought European backing Thursday after vowing to resume strikes on Russian oil refineries despite US President Donald Trump’s demands to stop. Tensions between Kyiv and Washington have escalated in recent days over sanctions, energy infrastructure attacks and restrictions on satellite communications.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/28bbd5dc-c8d5-11f1-aec7-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/80c62e6fc13f8d6a5641fe9e16da5b4e0ca12147.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/28bbd5dc-c8d5-11f1-aec7-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/80c62e6fc13f8d6a5641fe9e16da5b4e0ca12147.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fd8e39fa-c8ec-11f1-a26b-7beb10019f07</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:06:00 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/28bbd5dc-c8d5-11f1-aec7-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/80c62e6fc13f8d6a5641fe9e16da5b4e0ca12147.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>A propos</category><title>Sally Rooney's books cannot be sold in UK amid Palestine Action ban, publisher says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261015-sally-rooney-books-cannot-be-sold-in-uk-amid-palestine-action-ban-publisher</link><description>
Irish author Sally Rooney can no longer sell her books in the UK because of her support for the activist group Palestine Action, her publisher Faber said on Wednesday. Rooney has previously expressed her support for the group, which was banned as a "terrorist" organisation by the UK government in July 2025. It is not banned in Ireland, where Rooney lives. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Alan Greene, Professor of Constitutional Law and Human Rights at the Birmingham Law School.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5b769a14-c940-11f1-8e34-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-c3daade0.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5b769a14-c940-11f1-8e34-2d1c143cdef3/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-c3daade0.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">82159a16-c8dd-11f1-aa7d-07fd22e88b92</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:15:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Sharon GAFFNEY</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'It is clear that sooner or later we will have European casualties', Romanian MEP</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/it-is-clear-that-sooner-or-later-we-will-have-european-casualties-romanian-mep</link><description>
Rescuers searched on Thursday for seven missing sailors after drones struck two chemical tankers near Romania's Black Sea coast, setting them ablaze and raising fresh security concerns along a vital shipping route used by Ukraine. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Europe editor Armen Georgian, Nicolae Stefanuta, Romanian MEP and Co-Chair of the Group of the Greens, says that the Danube delta region is facing a more intense threat from Russia than Baltic States and that "it is clear that sooner or later we will have European casualties".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc7eaac2-c8d2-11f1-b063-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-211432-211932-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc7eaac2-c8d2-11f1-b063-638c1c1f5fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-211432-211932-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c1b2e1d4-c8d2-11f1-925f-cb689c3210d5</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:03:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Donald Trump 'openly financing Russia's war with Ukraine', Nobel peace laureate says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-openly-financing-russia-s-war-with-ukraine-nobel-peace-laureate-says</link><description>
Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, Nobel Peace laureate Oleksandra Matviichuk, Director of the Centre for Civil Liberties, says that with the diesel-supply deal with Moscow Donald Trump "is openly financing this war, by lifting sanctions is providing Russia with opportunities to earn more money" adding that "extra money will be converted in rockets and drones and additional deaths among the civilian population".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6dc8c71c-c8cf-11f1-b194-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-210633-211324-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6dc8c71c-c8cf-11f1-b194-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-210633-211324-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">72e458d8-c8cf-11f1-b211-61fe1cac82d8</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:48:10 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Seven missing off Romania after latest Black Sea drone attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/seven-missing-off-romania-after-latest-black-sea-drone-attacks</link><description>
Romania reported seven people missing on Thursday after two drone attacks on ships in the Black Sea, where several vessels have been hit recently in suspected fallout from the Ukraine war. The attacks are the latest in a series off the coast of Romania and neighbouring Bulgaria in recent weeks. FRANCE 24's Eliza Herbert reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d4a8504-c8c9-11f1-bf1b-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-203417-203608-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8d4a8504-c8c9-11f1-bf1b-4dd8ac2cf3bf/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261015-203417-203608-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">96ab9714-c8c9-11f1-8c3c-27acdd5cac97</guid><pubDate>Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:04:12 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
